{{Cyrillic character info|hex=45f|name=CYRILLIC SMALL LETTER DZHE}}
==Translingual==
[[Image:Cyrillic letter Dzhe.png|right|thumb|Cyrillic letter '''џ''' (''dzhe'')]]

===Etymology===
[[Image:GlagolitsaTsi.gif|Glagolitic letter Ⱌ (''tsi''), presumed to be the origin of Cyrillic letters ц (''ts'') and џ (''dž'')]]
Presumed to be a modification of [[ц]] (''ts''), itself presumed to be a modification of Glagolitic letter [[Ⱌ]] (''tsi'').  First recorded use in modern form is the 15th century [[w:Romanian Cyrillic alphabet|Romanian Cyrillic alphabet]].

===Letter===
{{infl|mul|letter|lower case||upper case|Џ|italic|[[џ|''џ'']]|upper case italic|[[Џ|''Џ'']]}}

# a Cyrillic letter of corresponding to the [[digraph]]s {{term|дж|tr=dzh}} or {{term|чж|tr=chzh}} or the letters {{term|җ|tr=zhj}}, {{term|ҷ|tr=chj}}, or {{term|ӂ|tr=dzh}}

----

==Macedonian==

===Etymology===
From Serbian Cyrillic letter [[џ#Serbian|џ]] (''dž''), adopted in 1945 by the Central Committee of [[w:League of Communists of Yugoslavia|the Communist Party of Yugoslavia]].

===Letter===
{{infl|mk|letter|lower case||upper case|Џ|italic|[[џ|''џ'']]|upper case italic|[[Џ|''Џ'']]}}

# The thirtieth letter of the Macedonian [[Cyrillic]] alphabet. Its name is {{term|џ|tr=dž}} and it has a similar sound to the English '''dg''' in ''do'''dg'''e''. It is preceded by [[ч|Ч]] and followed by [[ш|Ш]].

----

==Serbian==

===Pronunciation===
* {{qualifier|phoneme}} {{IPA|/dʒ/|lang=sr}}

===Etymology===
From [[џ#Translingual|џ]] of the 15th century [[w:Romanian Cyrillic alphabet|Romanian Cyrillic alphabet]], first used by Serbian scribes in the 17th century and part of [[w:Vuk Stefanović Karadžić|Vuk Stefanović Karadžić’s]] Cyrillic alphabet reform.

===Letter===
{{infl|sr|letter|lower case||upper case|Џ}}

# The 29th letter of the [[Serbian Cyrillic alphabet]].

====Usage notes====
Its name is {{term|џ|tr=dž}} and it has a similar sound to the English '''dg''' in ''do'''dg'''e''.

====See also====
* Previous letter: [[ч#Serbian|ч]]
* Next letter: [[ш#Serbian|ш]]

